22:22:24,677 root DEBUG {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You will be given a SQL query and some strategies to rewrite the given SQL query. Your task is to summarize the provided query rewrite strategies into one paragraph.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '\nSQL Query:\n```sql\nwith ss as\n (select ca_county,d_qoy, d_year,sum(ss_ext_sales_price) as store_sales\n from store_sales,date_dim,customer_address, item\n where ss_sold_date_sk = d_date_sk\n  and ss_addr_sk=ca_address_sk\n  and ss_item_sk = i_item_sk\n  and i_color IN (\'mint\', \'thistle\')\n  and i_manager_id BETWEEN 13 and 32\n  and ss_list_price between 107 and 121\n  and ca_state in (\'KS\',\'ND\')\n group by ca_county,d_qoy, d_year),\n ws as\n (select ca_county,d_qoy, d_year,sum(ws_ext_sales_price) as web_sales\n from web_sales,date_dim,customer_address, item\n where ws_sold_date_sk = d_date_sk\n  and ws_bill_addr_sk=ca_address_sk\n  and ws_item_sk = i_item_sk\n  and i_color IN (\'mint\', \'thistle\')\n  and i_manager_id BETWEEN 13 and 32\n  and ws_list_price between 107 and 121\n  and ca_state in (\'KS\',\'ND\')\ngroup by ca_county,d_qoy, d_year)\n select\n        ss1.ca_county\n       ,ss1.d_year\n       ,ws2.web_sales/ws1.web_sales web_q1_q2_increase\n       ,ss2.store_sales/ss1.store_sales store_q1_q2_increase\n       ,ws3.web_sales/ws2.web_sales web_q2_q3_increase\n       ,ss3.store_sales/ss2.store_sales store_q2_q3_increase\n from\n        ss ss1\n       ,ss ss2\n       ,ss ss3\n       ,ws ws1\n       ,ws ws2\n       ,ws ws3\n where\n    ss1.d_qoy = 1\n    and ss1.d_year = 1998\n    and ss1.ca_county = ss2.ca_county\n    and ss2.d_qoy = 2\n    and ss2.d_year = 1998\n and ss2.ca_county = ss3.ca_county\n    and ss3.d_qoy = 3\n    and ss3.d_year = 1998\n    and ss1.ca_county = ws1.ca_county\n    and ws1.d_qoy = 1\n    and ws1.d_year = 1998\n    and ws1.ca_county = ws2.ca_county\n    and ws2.d_qoy = 2\n    and ws2.d_year = 1998\n    and ws1.ca_county = ws3.ca_county\n    and ws3.d_qoy = 3\n    and ws3.d_year =1998\n    and case when ws1.web_sales > 0 then ws2.web_sales/ws1.web_sales else null end\n       > case when ss1.store_sales > 0 then ss2.store_sales/ss1.store_sales else null end\n    and case when ws2.web_sales > 0 then ws3.web_sales/ws2.web_sales else null end\n       > case when ss2.store_sales > 0 then ss3.store_sales/ss2.store_sales else null end\n order by web_q2_q3_increase;\n```\n\nQuery Rewrite Strategies:\nQuery Rewrite 1:\n"""The query rewrite process involves evaluating the constant arithmetic expressions in the `SELECT` list and replacing them with literal values. For example, the expression `/($19(ws_ext_sales_price), $15(ws_ext_sales_price))` is evaluated to a constant value and replaced with that value in the rewritten query. This simplification does not affect the nullability of the expression, as required by the rule. The rewritten query is then executed with the simplified expressions, which can improve performance and reduce the complexity of the query."""\n\nQuery Rewrite 2:\n"""The rewritten query applies the following changes:\n* Combines multiple subqueries into a single query.\n* Applies aggregate functions and `GROUP BY` to the data source.\n* Simplifies the `SELECT` clause by removing unnecessary columns and expressions.\n\nThe rewritten query is more efficient and easier to maintain than the original query."""'}], 'response': "Here's a summary of the provided SQL query rewrite strategies in one paragraph:\n\nThe first strategy involves simplifying constant arithmetic expressions in the SELECT list by evaluating them and replacing them with literal values, which can improve performance and reduce complexity. The second strategy combines multiple subqueries into a single query, applies aggregate functions and GROUP BY to the data source, and simplifies the SELECT clause by removing unnecessary columns and expressions, resulting in a more efficient and easier-to-maintain rewritten query.", 'time': 5.070514917373657}
